# Project documentation

Read root `AGENTS.md` and applicable nested instructions at the start of every
project prompt. Its documentation requirements are the canonical project rules.

For every file-changing task or completed implementation/setup/verification step,
use `.agents/skills/project-documentation/SKILL.md` and its linked deep documentation
standard. Read the affected reference through `docs/README.md` before changing it.

Keep meaningful function/class contracts adjacent to definitions and explain
affected cross-module behavior in the focused `docs/reference/` guide. Update
documentation and `docs/WORK_LOG.md` after each coherent step, before the next.
A file list, one-line purpose label, generated schema or log alone is insufficient.

Maintain affected source-backed Mermaid and SVG views using the documentation
skill's visual standard. Run diagram consistency checks and inspect actual output;
parse success alone cannot establish a readable, accurate diagram.

Before reporting completion, review affected paths against source-backed docs and
validate relevant links/examples/inline contracts. Preserve honest evidence and
approved scope. This entry point delegates details to AGENTS.md and the skill;
do not maintain a conflicting second copy of their policy here.
